 "inference": [
  "Class_7d3d8a5c is the damage-resistance effect class whose Field_658381bd L3315 named a damage-received multiplier by its registry-linked siblings; on that reading downed soldiers take 0.45 (bullets, crawling) or 0.05 (bullets and explosives) of normal damage, and an AI branch uses 2.0.",
  "The 0/1 ApplyAffector argument probably picks the list entry (Flak: one entry, argument 0).",
  "The Remove effects undo the modifiers by tag.",
  "None of the stored values equals 0.8, so EA's 20% is not read directly from these numbers; a different layer, or a different state (man-down rather than crawling), may produce it."
 ],
 "unresolved": [
  "Which entry (index 0 or 1) the ApplyAffector argument selects is inferred from Flak (one entry, argument 0); no multi-entry known-answer control exists.",
  "Meaning of the second ApplyAffector arguments and of the SELECT condition (Granite_StimBeingFired or an unnamed function fac8a68e) is unread.",
  "Whether HealthState / mandown type 0 (crawling) or 1 (man-down) triggers each call: the switch variable t32a4 is partly traced only.",
  "Runtime composition with armor, flak and plates (CeramicArmor and SoftArmor graphs reference the _Remove affector): needs capture of bodies 51fb26880d967f69 and bf4b65b03a70d55d.",
  "Native consumer of Class_7d3d8a5c multipliers not located; EA's 20% is not found in any stored value."
 ],
 "siteImpact": "None now. The site models no downed enemies. Conditional: if the crawling/man-down state is ever modelled, damage to a downed soldier would use these effects, but the 0.05 / 0.45 values do not reproduce EA's 20% line, so no number should be entered until the in-game test below is run.",
